<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kizlyar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kizlyar is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/terek-river">Terek River</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caspian-sea">Caspian Sea</a>. Founded as a Russian fortress in 1735, it anchored the eastern end of the Caucasian fortified line and became a trading town with Armenian and Georgian merchants, known for its wine and brandy. In 1996 Chechen fighters raided the town and took hundreds of hostages.</p></div>
